In article <1723@grivel.une.edu.au> scavanag@neumann.une.edu.au (Steven Cavanagh) writes:
>I've just cleaned out the castle level and am now trying to level
>teleport to level 50. I've been back through all the levels
>looking for a level teleport trap with no success (I'm SURE there
>was at least one there somewhere).

If I recall correctly, most level teleport traps disappear after they've
been used once.  You need to find it and not use it in order to be able
to use it effectively later.  Another hint:  Try searching for secret
doors where you find random scribblings near a wall in a room.

>I've tried using my wand
>of teleport on myself when I'm confused, but the wand just does
>strange things.

Wands do absolutely nothing different when you're confused (although what
you see or the message it gives may be slightly different).  Scrolls are
what act totally different when you're confused ("Being confused, you
mispronounce the words on this scroll.").

>I've even tried zapping that last charge out of my
>wand of wishing and wishing for a scroll of teleport, and the damn
>thing gives me fire or identify or some rubbish. How come some
>people wish for scrolls of recharging and get it? I've tried that
>and it doesn't work. I'm pretty sure the wand's not cursed, too.

Sounds like you're having a problem with exact wording.  You need to wish
for exactly what the item is.  I believe that a scroll of teleport is
a "scroll of teleportation," or more properly in this situation, a
"cursed scroll of teleportation" (since a cursed one will level teleport
you).  Also, it's a "scroll of charging," not a "scroll of recharging."

